# Module 2

Since we installed a new instance of the server, I changed the computer name to be something more manageable. 
It is good practice to name your servers, we can do so by clicking on the server name and going to change name to ny-DC-01. 
Usually, servers are named based on location and DC stands for domain controller. 

Our domain controller is going to act as the central server that is able to manage user access, verify credentials, etc.
An AD forest is the highest level of organization in AD. Each forest shares a single database, a single global address list and a security boundary. 
By default, a user or administrator in one forest cannot access another forest. One single AD configuration can contain more than one domain, and the tier above the domain the AD forest. 

By creating a new computer name, the VM is going to reboot for those changes to take effect and now I can go ahead and install Active Directory. 
Using the Roles and Feature Wizard tool, I am able to select the server I created with the new name of NY-DC-01.techorg1.com
The roles we are installing would AD Domain Services, DNS, and File and Storage Services. The features being installed are
group policy management and other Features that are automatically installed.

Once those features are installed, I clicked on promoting this server to a domain controller, and a installation wizard opens up
and we are given three options to choose how we want to deploy AD. I clicked on the Add a new forest option.
An AD forest is the highest level of organization in AD. Each forest shares a single database, a single global address list and a security boundary. 
By default, a user or administrator in one forest cannot access another forest. 
One single AD configuration can contain more than one domain, and the tier above the domain the AD forest. 

In the Active Directory Domain Services Configuration Wizard, Domain NetBIOS Name is the short, legacy name used by older Windows systems and applications to identify the domain.
ad.company.local = AD, contoso.com = CONTOSO
When you promote a server to a domain controller and create a new domain, the wizard typically automatically suggests a NetBIOS name based on the first label of the domain name.
In the adding roles and features wizard tool, we selected Active Directory Domain Services which added other tools by default. 
When the process finished, we have to promote the server we created (not the VM) to a domain controller by adding a new forest or highest level of an org in AD. 
